 outcome="Prepare a five-minute speech into short-line notes, rehearse it with numbers, and review it against the rubric with the devices of this course.",
 intro="Churchill wrote that rhetorical power is cultivated, with a natural base developed by practice, and that the orator must be swayed by what he says. The capstone applies that to a five-minute speech through planned rehearsal.",
